[30.115974, "o", "cat /root/.claude/skills/usgs-data-download/* 2>/dev/null | head -50\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[30.117205, "o", "---\r\nname: usgs-data-download\r\ndescription: Download water level data from USGS using the dataretrieval package. Use when accessing real-time or historical streamflow data, downloading gage height or discharge measurements, or working with USGS station IDs.\r\nlicense: MIT\r\n---\r\n\r\n# USGS Data Download Guide\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\n\r\nThis guide covers downloading water level data from USGS using the `dataretrieval` Python package. USGS maintains thousands of stream gages across the United States that record water levels at 15-minute intervals.\r\n\r\n## Installation"]
[30.117278, "o", "\r\n```bash\r\npip install dataretrieval\r\n```\r\n\r\n## nwis Module (Recommended)\r\n\r\nThe NWIS module is reliable and straightforward for accessing gage height data.\r\n```python\r\nfrom dataretrieval import nwis\r\n\r\n# Get instantaneous values (15-min intervals)\r\ndf, meta = nwis.get_iv(\r\n    sites='<station_id>',\r\n    start='<start_date>',\r\n    end='<end_date>',\r\n    parameterCd='00065'\r\n)\r\n\r\n# Get daily values\r\ndf, meta = nwis.get_dv(\r\n    sites='<station_id>',\r\n    start='<start_date>',\r\n    end='<end_date>',\r\n    parameterCd='00060'\r\n)\r\n\r\n# Get site information\r\ninfo, meta = nwis.get_info(sites='<station_id>')\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Parameter Codes\r\n\r\n| Code | Parameter | Unit | Description |\r\n|------|-----------|------|-------------|\r\n| `00065` | Gage height | feet | Water level above datum |\r\n| `00060` | Discharge | cfs | Streamflow volume |\r\n\r\n"]
[30.117502, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@90924ac9ce32:~# "]
[30.344967, "i", "python3 -c \"import sys; print(sys.executable)\"\n"]
[30.345246, "o", "python3 -c \"import sys; print(sys.executable)\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[30.355367, "o", "/usr/bin/python3\r\n"]
[30.357539, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@90924ac9ce32:~# "]
[39.199948, "i", "python3 -c \"import dataretrieval; print('dataretrieval installed')\"\n"]
[39.20064, "o", "python3 -c \"import dataretrieval; print('dataretrieval installed')\""]
[39.200752, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[40.012292, "o", "dataretrieval installed\r\n"]
[40.199066, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@90924ac9ce32:~# "]
[50.651532, "i", "cat > /root/test_station.py << 'EOF'\nfrom dataretrieval import nwis\nimport pandas as pd\n\n# Test with first station\nstation_id = '04031000'\n\n# Get daily values for April 1-7, 2025\ndf, meta = nwis.get_dv(\n    sites=station_id,\n    start='2025-04-01',\n    end='2025-04-07',\n    parameterCd='00060'  # Discharge/streamflow\n)\n\nprint(\"Data shape:\", df.shape)\nprint(\"\\nColumns:\", df.columns.tolist())\nprint(\"\\nFirst few rows:\")\nprint(df.head(10))\nprint(\"\\nMetadata:\")\nprint(meta)\n\n# Try to get site info including flood stage\ninfo, info_meta = nwis.get_info(sites=station_id)\nprint(\"\\n\\nSite info:\")\nprint(info)\nEOF\n"]
